<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Yan of Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 328–286 BCE</span> · Also known as Dai Yan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Yan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> was the last ruler of the state of Song in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>, taking power around 328 BCE and later assuming the royal title. He fought aggressive wars against his neighbours, conquering the small state of Teng, and Chinese histories portray him as a tyrant. In 286 BCE Qi, with Wei and Chu, destroyed Song and divided its lands.</p></div>
